# UI structure

Static export only (`output: 'export'`). No `getServerSideProps`, no `getInitialProps`, no `pages/api`, no server-only Next APIs. Brand tokens come from `packages/ui/tokens.css` through `packages/ui/tailwind.preset.ts`. Specs: `docs/design/tokens.md`, `docs/design/components.md`, `docs/design/responsive.md`. `design-system/self-study-ai/` is deprecated. No raw hex in components. No invented marketing copy.

## Where files go

- `packages/ui/src/` — shared controls. Flat. No subfolders. No `index.ts` barrel. Import `@self-study/ui/Button`.
- `apps/web/src/components/` and `apps/landing/src/components/` — app-specific controls. Flat. No subfolders.
- `sections/` — page blocks that compose components. Flat. A section does not import another section.
- `pages/` — Next.js routes. Thin. Set the title and render sections.
- `hooks/` — data and behavior. `apps/web` API access goes through `lib/api-client.ts` only.
- `lib/` — client, logger, small helpers.

`apps/web` and `apps/landing` never import each other. They share a component only by moving it into `packages/ui`. Do not copy a component from one app into the other.

## Direction

`pages -> sections -> components`. Components do not import sections, pages, or data hooks. If two sections need the same thing, extract a component.

## Components

- One component per file. PascalCase file name. Named export. Props interface `<Component>Props`.
- Presentational. Text and handlers come in through props. Accept `className` and forward `data-testid`. Form controls use `forwardRef`.
- Variants are props, not duplicate components.
- Search the flat folder before adding a file. Extend an existing component with a prop when it fits.
- Accessible by default: visible label, keyboard support, visible focus, 44px minimum target. Cursor pointer on clickable elements. Hover uses opacity or color, not a transform that shifts layout. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- No raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, or `<table>` in a section or page.

Shared controls that must stay reusable: Button, Input, Select, Textarea, Toggle, Modal, DataTable, StatusChip, EmptyState, ErrorState, ToastProvider, Loader, Sidebar, AppShell. Toast is custom (no toast library), mounted once in `pages/_app.tsx`, triggered with `useToast()`. Tones: success, error, warning, info. Loader is the loading state. ErrorState and EmptyState are the failure and empty states.

## Design system

Read `docs/design/components.md` before changing a shared control, and `docs/design/responsive.md` before changing layout. Add a token in `packages/ui/tokens.css` before using a new color, size, radius, shadow, or space. Do not edit `design-system/self-study-ai/`.
